## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates the ability to design governance-aware AI copilots that enforce enterprise privacy policies, implement policy-as-code, and ensure auditable, defensible decisions in multi-tenant environments.

## Key Concepts
- Azure OpenAI integration with API Management for secure API exposure
- Cognitive Search knowledge base grounding against versioned Azure Blob storage
- Policy-as-code modules for privacy, consent, and data retention enforcement
- Per-tenant Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) via Azure Active Directory
- Comprehensive auditable logging in Azure Data Lake or equivalent storage
- End-to-end test harness for validation across all components

## Code Example
```javascript
function evaluatePolicy(request, kb, policy) {
  const redactedRequest = redactPII(request, policy.piiRules);
  const groundedContext = await searchKnowledgeBase(redactedRequest, kb);
  const consentCheck = validateConsent(redactedRequest, policy.consentRules);
  const retentionCheck = validateRetention(redactedRequest, policy.retentionRules);

  if (!consentCheck.valid || !retentionCheck.valid) {
    return { decision: 'DENY', rationale: [...consentCheck.reasons, ...retentionCheck.reasons] };
  }

  const decision = await openai.chat.completions.create({
    messages: [{ role: 'system', content: policy.determinationPrompt },
               { role: 'user', content: JSON.stringify({ request: redactedRequest, context: groundedContext }) }]
  });

  return parseDecision(decision);
}
```

